<title>UK: European cotton trade at a minimum.</title>
<headline>European cotton trade at a minimum.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most spinning mills were closed and holiday influences kept trading interest to a minimum throughouit most European raw cotton markets.</p>
<p>The underlying sentiment with regard to prices remains firm with the approach of the new year, traders said.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
